Subject: [PATCH] hosts/hermes-ci-runners: runner AMI source and probe (#132)

* hosts/hermes-ci-runners: tfgar probe (Packer AMI, multi-runner v8, fail-closed IMDS hook, probe lane)

* actionlint: allow tfgar-probe label

* tfgar probe: fix review t_01a180ac R1-R3

R1: IMDS readback probes the token PUT with curl -f (disabled IMDS answers 403,
not connection refused); test stub models 403; workflow assertion checks http_code.
R2: remove the amazon-ssm-agent snap from the AMI and assert it is gone.
R3: bidirectionalLabelMatch so jobs sharing only 'self-hosted' don't scale probe VMs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* tfgar probe: AMI build + plan fixes

packer: pass RUNNER_VERSION through sudo (execute_command needs {{ .Vars }}); create /tmp/ghr-files before
the file provisioner. terraform: plan-time ARNs for the AMI SSM parameter and IMDS hook policy (module counts
off them); ignore lambda zips and plan files. bootstrap: serve-manifest.py for the App manifest click;
store-github-app.sh base64 portable to macOS. Built ami-0ae486be3eb34e4e1; plan: 69 to add.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* tfgar probe: R4 review nits (portable probe-branch rewrite, two-pass apply doc)

R4 review of 843d91b42a: APPROVE. make-probe-branch.sh used GNU-only sed; rewrite in python.
README: targeted first pass needs -var ami_id and a fresh plan afterwards.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* tfgar probe: module SSM root /hermes-ci so broker aws.write.hermes covers it

Plan unchanged at 69 creates; no /github-action-runners paths remain.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* tfgar probe AMI: bubblewrap + apparmor_restrict_unprivileged_userns=0, asserted at build

e2e-upgrade and desktop-update lanes failed on the docker runners (read-only sysctl => bwrap unusable,
runs 40481801409, 40637455814). The build now fails unless bwrap works for the runner user.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* tfgar probe: module roles carry the ci-runners-boundary permissions boundary

The broker's aws.write.hermes scope may only create/modify hermes-ci-* roles that carry
policy/ci-runners-boundary (Metta-AI/metta#29731), so an approved session can't mint persistent access.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* tfgar probe: IMDS hook policy uses StringEquals aws:ARN like the module

CreatePolicy rejected the ArnLike form with MalformedPolicyDocument (legacy parsing) on the first apply.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* tfgar probe: role_path / so module role ARNs match role/hermes-ci-*

The webhook Lambda role was created under /hermes-ci/ and the broker write role's IAM carve-out
(role/hermes-ci-*) denied CreateRole.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* hermes-ci-runners image: fixes from the first full probe

- rustup/cargo symlinked into /usr/local/bin (job PATH lacks ~/.cargo/bin)
- clang baked (pm-bundle builds pilk's C extension with it)
- apt lists kept (jobs apt-get install without update, as on hosted images)
- no ayatana appindicator (conflicts with rust-tests' libappindicator3-dev)
- packer no longer passes HOME through sudo; bake fails on root-owned files in ~ubuntu

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* hermes-ci-runners: pass repo lint (env bash shebangs, no /tmp literals, subprocess timeout)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* hermes-ci-runners: job_retry on the probe runner, cap 6 -> 12

A probe run left two e2e-upgrade shards queued for hours: at the runner cap the
scale-up event was dropped and nothing relaunched for them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* hermes-ci-runners: route ci-fast to an ephemeral fast group

First real label after the probe passed. Jobs asking for exactly
[self-hosted, ci-fast] scale up c7a/c6a/m7a.large spot VMs (cap 8) from the
same AMI and fail-closed IMDS hook; the old ci-fast boxes stay registered as
fallback. Probe and fast share one runner_base.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* hermes-ci-runners: pause the fast group (cap 0)

Canary: all 21 ci-fast jobs in 10 min went to the old boxes, which take a job
in seconds; each tfgar VM booted and idled. Shared labels give the new group
only overflow, so it stays paused until a label only it serves.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* hermes-ci-runners: fast group serves a tfgar-fast label only, cap 8

Workflows move onto it by switching runs-on to [self-hosted, tfgar-fast], a few
at a time; rollback is reverting that workflow PR. The old ci-fast boxes stay
untouched.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* hermes-ci-runners: hermes-hub overflow group replaces the fast group

On-demand VMs for jobs asking for exactly [self-hosted, hermes-hub], the label
the old on-demand hub boxes also serve. A 45 s webhook delay plus the queued-job
check launch a VM only for a job the old boxes left waiting. Workflows and old
boxes are unchanged; rollback is hub_max_runners = 0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* hermes-ci-runners: hub cap 2 until the on-demand vCPU quota rises

Old boxes use 80 of the 96 on-demand standard vCPUs; over the quota CreateFleet
fails VcpuLimitExceeded and scale-up drops the job instead of retrying.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* hermes-ci-runners: enable the queued-job check

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* hermes-ci-runners: region-independent apt sources; drop the moved terraform

Baked package lists failed in us-east-1 because cloud-init repoints apt at the boot
region's EC2 mirror. Pin archive.ubuntu.com and preserve the sources; the bake now
asserts both. The stack moved to metta devops/tf/hermes-ci-runners and the one here
is destroyed, so terraform/ and its state bootstrap go.

